    {
      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "To find the value of \\(23^2 + 2(23)(2) + 2^2\\), we can use the formula for the square of a binomial, which states:\n\n\\[\n(a + b)^2 = a^2 + 2ab + b^2\n\\]\n\nIn this problem, \\(a = 23\\) and \\(b = 2\\). Let's apply this formula step by step:\n\n1. Identify \\(a\\) and \\(b\\):\n   \\[\n   a = 23, \\quad b = 2\n   \\]\n\n2. Calculate \\(a^2\\):\n   \\[\n   a^2 = 23^2 = 529\n   \\]\n\n3. Calculate \\(2ab\\):\n   \\[\n   2ab = 2 \\cdot 23 \\cdot 2 = 92\n   \\]\n\n4. Calculate \\(b^2\\):\n   \\[\n   b^2 = 2^2 = 4\n   \\]\n\n5. Combine these results using the binomial expansion formula:\n   \\[\n   a^2 + 2ab + b^2 = 529 + 92 + 4\n   \\]\n\n6. Perform the addition:\n   \\[\n   529 + 92 = 621\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   621 + 4 = 625\n   \\]\n\nTherefore, the value of \\(23^2 + 2(23)(2) + 2^2\\) is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{625}\n\\]",
